WEBVTT

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:43.080
It's no good.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:45.080
The way it is right now...

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:51.840
If it keeps running the way it is right now,

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:53.310
that Z will...

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:55.500
definitely...

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.060
die.

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:07.650
<i>New Machine</i>

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:15.410
Ok, last shot.

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:18.760
That was great.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:19.620
You did a good job.

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:21.050
Thank you very much.

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:25.650
Take care of the rest for me.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:26.460
Yes.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:28.840
Thanks again, Ishida-sensei.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:31.050
I'll see you next time.

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:51.150
Kitami-san.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:00.330
Please tell me.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:03.900
The other day, you said the Z was going to die.

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:05.020
Was that true?

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:06.930
Was it?

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:10.430
It is true.

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:11.830
Why?

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:13.120
What's it matter to you?

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:14.340
That's...

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:16.420
Akio-kun...

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:19.850
Would you tell that Z's driver?

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:23.870
Please come with me.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.560
H-Hey!

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:38.010
<i>Maybe we'll just have to overhaul, Kou-chan.</i>

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:43.500
<i>But I'm not sure if there's anyone who can take
apart this engine and put it back together.</i>

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:45.910
<i>I know I can't, Akio.</i>

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.550
How did you know my school?

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:10.820
Yokohama 33, ‘T’ 53-681.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:13.730
I looked up the plate at the DMV.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:17.990
I didn't think you were a high school
student living alone, though.

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:21.280
Are you the one who built that Z...?

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:23.910
It wasn't running like it's supposed to.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:26.280
Yeah.

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:39.790
Even if you tweak the carburetor and ignition,
or look at the tappet, it won't help.

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:42.560
If you keep driving it the way it is now,

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:44.510
it will definitely die.

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:47.140
A full overhaul?

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:49.090
It's a machine, after all.

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:53.110
You'll have to take apart the engine completely
and get rid of the worn parts.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:54.440
And then...

00:04:56.190 --> 00:05:01.830
Well, there's only one person who can take
that baby apart and put it back together.

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:06.250
But that man has no intention to build another engine.

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:14.880
Kitami-san, you're a pretty mean old man.

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:19.840
You won't tune my R and you won't even fix that Z.

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:22.560
Of course not.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:26.320
If I killed a beautiful little girl like you,

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:28.180
it would leave a bitter after-taste.

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:31.050
Then, please fix that Z.

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:32.050
I can't do that.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:37.940
Besides, I think I'll get an order for a new car very soon.

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:40.830
Eh? A new car?

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:47.240
Ishida-sensei.

00:05:50.150 --> 00:05:50.830
Hey.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:52.750
Were you two on a date?

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:56.490
I can't have you parking something so flashy right here.

00:05:57.740 --> 00:05:58.380
Thanks.

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:01.010
This was the "new car" you were talking about?

00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:02.670
I wonder...

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:05.560
Please, Kitami-san.

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:09.310
Make this Testa' faster than that Z.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:13.320
Faster than that Z?

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:14.560
That'll be pretty hard.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:21.070
I've built many cars in the past but that Z is truly special.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:23.860
There are parts even I don't quite understand.

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:27.460
It was really born just to drive.

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:33.780
This thing costs over $200,000, right?

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:34.880
Yeah...

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:38.590
Then for starters, why don't you
bring me $100,000 for tuning it?

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:43.010
Ok.

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:49.940
You're going to put another $100K into
a car that already costs $200K?

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:55.520
And in exchange for that price, you will
be able to drive in front of that Z.

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:59.090
Or die in the process.

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:06.160
I hope you understand the machines Kitami
Jun puts together work like that.

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:13.870
L28 Kai Twin Turbo.

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:16.420
It's not extremely complicated.

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:19.800
We'll start by collecting the gaskets and washers.

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:21.330
And it's a carburetor-turbo, so...

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:24.050
If you take it apart, it'll be hard to restore the original settings.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:24.840
I know.

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:27.640
You're really gonna do this by yourself?

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:28.770
Yeah.

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:31.560
After all, it's my Z...

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:34.320
So I want to overhaul it with my own hands.

00:07:57.010 --> 00:07:59.440
Hey Akio, how's it going?

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:00.970
Good.

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:03.750
Are there any tools you need?

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:04.540
I'll loan it to you.

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:06.680
That's actually why I'm here.

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:08.560
It's pretty expensive if you try to buy it yourself.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:12.680
So you were relying on me from the start?

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:15.450
Take what you want from the garage.

00:08:15.690 --> 00:08:17.190
Thanks, Kou-chan.

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:33.750
Good evening, Akio-kun.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:36.410
Wanna go somewhere interesting?

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:38.750
Sorry, but I'm tired today.

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:42.800
Kitami-san's tuning the Testa' right now.

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:48.770
Over there.

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:52.710
He borrowed this factory just to tune it.

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:01.900
Good evening.

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:03.140
Sorry to interrupt.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:04.360
Is it ok?

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:05.440
To watch you a little?

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:12.120
Be my guest.

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:15.320
You're taking apart that Z by yourself?

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:16.080
Yeah.

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:18.350
I managed to take it apart.

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:20.140
What about the new parts?

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:22.750
For starters, the gaskets and washers.

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:25.880
And then?

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:27.310
I took everything apart.

00:09:27.850 --> 00:09:30.650
The turbine, cam and crank...

00:09:30.650 --> 00:09:33.670
You washed all the parts and cleaned them?

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:36.010
Yeah and greased it up.

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:39.300
Is that not good enough?

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:42.130
I wonder...

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:46.960
How much longer until you're done?

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:48.280
Another week.

00:09:48.970 --> 00:09:51.070
I'll be done by then, too.

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:05.040
<i>If I lane-change at over 250km/h,</i>

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:06.310
<i>the traction can't keep up.</i>

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:09.060
<i>And I want at least another 100hp.</i>

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:21.230
Whoa, you actually overhauled the whole engine?

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:22.190
Yeah.

00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:24.080
I did everything I could.

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:26.430
I'm impressed you did this much.

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:28.640
Alright, step on it.

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:29.150
Alright.

00:10:45.630 --> 00:10:46.500
Alright.

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:51.630
This is the last time I'll say it, I can't guarantee your safety.

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:53.260
I know.

00:10:53.990 --> 00:10:58.760
This car's been tuned by the tuner from Hell, Kitami Jun.

00:11:11.630 --> 00:11:13.300
Let's go, to Wangan.

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:27.310
I'm flattered, Kitami-san.

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:30.170
I didn't think you would ride next to me.

00:11:30.650 --> 00:11:32.730
I really can't take any responsibility.

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:34.680
Don't worry about it and step on it.

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:45.290
Amazing.

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:47.320
This car's great.

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:53.600
He's here.

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:55.280
That sounds like my Z.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:12:00.030
There, there... you sound great!

00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:09.130
<i>I don't want to drive in front of him...</i>

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:11.950
<i>If I can just keep up.</i>

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:16.060
<i>That's right, I just want to keep up with this Z.</i>

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:20.260
<i>It feels so strange.</i>

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:23.200
<i>I thought I cleaned myself.</i>

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:24.900
<i>Yet, here I am tuning cars again.</i>

00:12:27.630 --> 00:12:30.150
<i>Everything because of that Z.</i>

00:12:30.150 --> 00:12:34.110
<i>Thanks to you, I'm back in this world.</i>

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:44.320
Your eyes are fixed...

00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:46.330
is that Z still your favorite?

00:12:48.110 --> 00:12:50.290
Don't mind that and just step on it.

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:54.980
<i>Took it apart and cleaned it?</i>

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:58.110
<i>That's all it needed.</i>

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:02.780
<i>Yeah, drive like that.</i>

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:05.130
<i>Step on the gas more.</i>

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:08.170
<i>Harder, more! More!.</i>

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:15.150
<i>It didn't go well as a job.</i>

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:19.190
<i>I was up to my head in debt and my family ran away from me.</i>

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:22.700
<i>But that doesn't matter.</i>

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:28.290
<i>I'm just glad that there is someone
who can understand my cars!</i>

00:13:31.850 --> 00:13:33.330
<i>I'm shivering.</i>

00:13:33.770 --> 00:13:36.050
<i>You are truly an amazing car...</i>

00:13:36.520 --> 00:13:40.050
<i>Like you keep getting faster on your own.</i>

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:43.190
<i>You found a nice owner.</i>

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:50.480
I still can't catch up?

00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:52.020
Hey, are you ok?

00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:53.020
I'm fine.

00:14:20.310 --> 00:14:21.180
Are you hurt!?

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:40.810
I have to say, the newer the Porsche, the better.

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:43.050
Even stock tuned, they are fast enough.

00:14:43.050 --> 00:14:46.080
You sure put together a car that doesn't fit your style.

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:52.350
If you lane-change at over 250km/h, the rear loses control.

00:14:52.980 --> 00:14:54.050
And there's not enough power.

00:14:54.570 --> 00:15:00.630
To tell you the truth, I didn't think you would buy a new turbo.

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:03.970
Though I'm sure it's to race that Z...

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:10.140
But in the near future, we'll be working on everyday cars.

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:14.230
So, what I'm saying is... high tuned cars are...

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:15.560
I understand.

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:18.440
No, I mean...

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:21.320
Why don't you cut back on driving on Wangan?

00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:25.370
Thanks for everything until now, boss.

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:42.300
<i>It's a good car, but...</i>

00:15:42.630 --> 00:15:44.800
<i>In order for me to keep up with the Z on Wangan,</i>

00:15:45.230 --> 00:15:47.340
<i>everything has to go as I imagined.</i>

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:51.730
<i>It's no good...</i>

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:54.850
<i>I can't trust my life in this machine.</i>

00:15:57.990 --> 00:15:58.480
Yes?

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:04.990
Eh?! Ishida-sensei, you're hospitalized?

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:07.670
<i>I'm lonely so come visit me, Reina-chan.</i>

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:18.280
I'm not tuning your car, no matter how you ask, missy.

00:16:18.570 --> 00:16:20.290
Today isn't about that.

00:16:20.650 --> 00:16:22.790
Ishida-sensei has been hospitalized.

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:27.300
Man, dunno what to say...

00:16:27.620 --> 00:16:29.920
They found a tumor in my stomach.

00:16:30.270 --> 00:16:31.060
Tumor?

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:34.050
It's not like I wasn't expecting it, though.

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:36.440
How is it, Shima-sensei?

00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:38.390
There's no problem.

00:16:39.460 --> 00:16:41.000
Let's go with a laparoscopy.

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:41.730
<i> Laparoscopy is an operation performed in the abdomen or pelvis through small incisions (usually 0.5–1.5 cm) with the aid of a camera.</i>

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:45.730
I think he can be discharged within a week of the operation.

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:47.740
Come in.

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:50.910
Ho are you feeling?

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:53.190
I feel great.

00:16:53.190 --> 00:16:55.040
I could get discharged right now.

00:16:56.460 --> 00:17:02.090
Oh, he's going to be the director of the department
of surgery at this hospital... Shima-sensei.

00:17:03.010 --> 00:17:04.160
BlackBird.

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:05.200
What?

00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:10.800
<i>This man is...</i>

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:12.940
<i>Kitami Jun!</i>

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:20.590
G-Good evening.

00:17:22.030 --> 00:17:24.250
I know I'm a nuisance, but...

00:17:24.250 --> 00:17:25.520
I don't mind.

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:28.660
<i>No matter how similar they are,</i>

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:30.600
<i>this person isn't my brother.</i>

00:17:32.210 --> 00:17:33.020
Get in.

00:17:33.020 --> 00:17:35.160
You came to see this Z, right?

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:44.040
<i>I want to sit in this Z forever...</i>

00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:45.460
<i>But...</i>

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:49.500
<i>Even if he drives the same car,</i>

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:51.050
<i>has the same name...</i>

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:53.680
<i>he still isn't my brother.</i>

00:17:54.600 --> 00:17:56.940
<i>But I feel like he's going to go somewhere far away,</i>

00:17:57.360 --> 00:17:59.970
<i>like my brother did, back then.</i>

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:05.030
<i>I get the same feeling around Tatsuya and some other people.</i>

00:18:05.590 --> 00:18:07.630
<i>Anyone with the need for speed.</i>

00:18:07.990 --> 00:18:10.750
<i>It seems like they'll just keep driving...
so far I can't see them anymore.</i>

00:18:10.750 --> 00:18:14.230
<i>Those who drive at unbelievable speeds...</i>

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:17.010
<i>Those attracted to this Z.</i>

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:26.170
Alright.

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:27.430
Assist me.

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:33.510
How are you feeling?

00:18:33.510 --> 00:18:35.130
I feel great.

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:36.970
I could get discharged right now.

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:40.560
If you don't push yourself that hard, it shouldn't take long.

00:18:40.900 --> 00:18:46.370
You're young, handsome, skilled and your
parents own another major hospital...

00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:47.930
You're amazing.

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:50.220
Born elite.

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:55.100
But, I think the Wangan is a little too
dangerous for relieving your stress.

00:18:55.440 --> 00:18:56.060
Ishida-san...

00:18:57.120 --> 00:19:00.190
After you're discharged, do you intend to keep following him?

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:01.090
Yep.

00:19:01.500 --> 00:19:05.000
I live to take girls' pictures and chase that Z.

00:19:05.510 --> 00:19:08.750
I'm sure you would do the same if you were in my position.

00:19:09.740 --> 00:19:13.050
Anyone bewitched by that Z would say the same.

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:19.600
In the end, the one most attracted to it may be you.

00:19:27.460 --> 00:19:28.750
<i>It's still not good.</i>

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:31.590
<i>I need to make some fine adjustments
between the steering and acceleration.</i>

00:19:33.180 --> 00:19:35.370
<i>The tuner from Hell, Kitami Jun.</i>

00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:37.320
<i>Maybe he could...</i>

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:44.500
Congratulations on your discharge, Ishida-sensei.

00:19:45.090 --> 00:19:46.920
Why, thank you.

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:50.000
Let's meet again, sensei.

00:19:55.800 --> 00:19:56.850
<i>Shima-sensei.</i>

00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:59.050
<i>Shima-sensei, you have a guest in the lobby.</i>

00:20:01.770 --> 00:20:03.020
Withdrawing from school?

00:20:03.480 --> 00:20:07.320
Yeah, Tatsuya always agreed...

00:20:07.710 --> 00:20:08.610
I want to study abroad.

00:20:09.030 --> 00:20:10.070
For about two years.

00:20:10.450 --> 00:20:14.070
Daddy was so happy, he said "go right now".

00:20:14.890 --> 00:20:16.770
My departure is one week from today.

00:20:16.770 --> 00:20:18.030
I was so surprised.

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:19.910
I think it's a good idea.

00:20:21.910 --> 00:20:24.420
Why don't you forget everything and have a good time?

00:20:25.030 --> 00:20:25.580
Ok.

00:20:26.020 --> 00:20:27.400
But before that...

00:20:27.890 --> 00:20:28.410
What is it?

00:20:29.590 --> 00:20:32.200
I wanted to see the Z one last time...

00:20:33.610 --> 00:20:35.740
Ok, I'll tag along.

00:20:45.790 --> 00:20:48.380
It didn't seem like anything was wrong,

00:20:48.670 --> 00:20:49.610
with your R.

00:20:50.690 --> 00:20:52.860
Really? It looked good to you?

00:20:53.320 --> 00:20:54.000
Yeah, it did.

00:20:54.470 --> 00:20:55.660
I'm going home now.

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:57.160
W-Wait a sec!

00:20:58.300 --> 00:20:59.120
I'm sorry...

00:20:59.530 --> 00:21:02.280
I actually wanted to ride with you, Akio-kun.

00:21:05.180 --> 00:21:06.540
Then, do you wanna have some tea?

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:08.530
Yeah!

00:21:10.860 --> 00:21:12.810
This is really the last time.

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:14.010
Yeah.

00:21:14.590 --> 00:21:17.630
He should probably be done with work by now, so...

00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:19.010
maybe he's at the garage.

00:21:28.110 --> 00:21:29.930
I'm sorry, but could you get him?

00:21:30.220 --> 00:21:31.890
Yeah, wait here.

00:21:48.930 --> 00:21:51.160
Eh!? Why is BlackBird here?

00:21:51.580 --> 00:21:52.710
I need to talk to you.

00:21:53.330 --> 00:21:54.800
Could you come outside?

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:03.500
It's Eriko!

00:22:03.500 --> 00:22:05.600
She had a spare key to that Z?

00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:10.110
S-She's fast!

00:22:10.570 --> 00:22:12.390
Is she really driving that?

00:22:15.450 --> 00:22:16.650
The harbor?

00:22:20.470 --> 00:22:21.860
She's driving towards the harbor?

00:22:22.110 --> 00:22:22.940
Don't tell me, she's...

00:22:29.020 --> 00:22:31.940
<i>Hey brother, what's this car called?</i>

00:22:32.240 --> 00:22:33.130
<i>Z.</i>

00:22:33.130 --> 00:22:34.960
<i>Fairlady Z.</i>

00:22:37.750 --> 00:22:38.860
<i>Can you fix it?</i>

00:22:39.160 --> 00:22:41.280
<i>Don't worry, leave it to me.</i>

00:22:41.280 --> 00:22:43.480
<i>When you fix it, let me ride in it first.</i>

00:22:43.480 --> 00:22:44.960
<i>Do you need help with anything?</i>

00:22:46.710 --> 00:22:48.070
<i>No, no... nothing.</i>

00:22:48.580 --> 00:22:51.780
<i>But, you like this car that much, Eriko?</i>

00:22:52.230 --> 00:22:54.810
<i>I just thought I heard this car calling me.</i>

00:22:55.340 --> 00:22:57.690
<i>"Help me. Fix me".</i>

00:23:01.010 --> 00:23:02.990
<i>I'm the one who found this car.</i>

00:23:03.590 --> 00:23:04.320
<i>That's why...!</i>

00:23:07.780 --> 00:23:09.170
She's going to sink it in the ocean?!

00:23:16.830 --> 00:23:19.400
D-Don't!!
